<h2 id="climate">Climate at a position</h2>
<p class="muted">
  Enter a numeric world seed and the climate-related world options, then click the map above (or type a position), to see the temperature,
  rainfall and geologic activity the world generator assigns there &mdash; and which wild plants and trees from this wiki's data can grow in that
  climate. This is a client-side port of the game's <em>realistic</em> climate generator (the seeded per-cell randomness plus the north&ndash;south
  temperature gradient), written against the game's own source. It runs entirely in your browser.
</p>

<div class="coverage-note">
  <p><strong>Approximate, not exact.</strong> The game warps the finished climate map with a
  simplex-noise "wobble" that this page does not reproduce, so a given block can be off by up to
  about 900 blocks' worth of climate. Terrain height (landforms) is not simulated either: use the
  height field to apply the game's altitude formula by hand. Only <strong>numeric</strong> seeds are
  supported; the game turns a text seed into a number in code that isn't available here.
  <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}sources/map/">Full details on what is and isn't ported &rarr;</a></p>
</div>

<form id="clForm" class="schematic-row-fields" onsubmit="return false">
  <label class="schematic-field">World seed (number) <input type="number" id="clSeed" value="12345" step="1" min="-2147483648" max="2147483647"></label>
  <label class="schematic-field">Starting climate
    <select id="clStart">
      <option value="default">Default (6 to 14 °C)</option>
      <option value="hot">Hot (28 to 32 °C)</option>
      <option value="warm">Warm (19 to 23 °C)</option>
      <option value="cool">Cool (-5 to 1 °C)</option>
      <option value="icy">Icy (-15 to -10 °C)</option>
    </select>
  </label>
  <label class="schematic-field">Polar&ndash;equator distance (blocks) <input type="number" id="clPolar" value="50000" step="1000" min="1000"></label>
  <label class="schematic-field">World size (blocks) <input type="number" id="clSize" value="1024000" step="1000" min="1000"></label>
  <label class="schematic-field">Global temperature &times; <input type="number" id="clTempMul" value="1" step="0.1" min="0"></label>
  <label class="schematic-field">Global precipitation &times; <input type="number" id="clRainMul" value="1" step="0.1" min="0"></label>
  <label class="schematic-field">Geologic activity <input type="number" id="clGeo" value="0.05" step="0.01" min="0.01"></label>
</form>
<form id="clPos" class="schematic-row-fields" onsubmit="return false">
  <label class="schematic-field">X (blocks from world center) <input type="number" id="clX" value="0" step="100"></label>
  <label class="schematic-field">Z (blocks from world center) <input type="number" id="clZ" value="0" step="100"></label>
  <label class="schematic-field">Height Y <input type="number" id="clY" value="125" step="1"></label>
</form>

<h3>Result</h3>
<ul id="clResults">
  <li id="clSpawn"></li>
  <li id="clTemp"></li>
  <li id="clRain"></li>
  <li id="clGeoOut"></li>
</ul>

<h3>Temperature around this position</h3>
<p class="muted">Sea-level temperature, 64&times;64 noise cells (each {{ 512 }} blocks wide), centered on the position above.
Blue is cold, red is hot; north is up.</p>
<canvas id="clMap" width="256" height="256" style="max-width:100%;image-rendering:pixelated;border:1px solid var(--border, #888)"></canvas>

<h3>Wild plants and trees that fit this climate</h3>
<p class="muted">Matched on temperature and rainfall at the height above only; each also has other conditions (fertility, forest density, terrain)
that this page doesn't model. Bands come from the same data as <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}crops/">Crops</a>,
<a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}trees/">Trees</a> and <a href="{{ ('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url }}fruit-trees/">Fruit Trees</a>.</p>
<p id="clSpawnCount"></p>
<table>
  <thead><tr><th>Kind</th><th>Name</th><th>Temperature (&deg;C)</th><th>Rainfall</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody id="clSpawnList"></tbody>
</table>

<script type="application/json" id="climateSpawns">[
{%- set first = true -%}
{%- for p in generated.blockPatches -%}
  {%- if p.minTemp != null or p.maxTemp != null or p.minRain != null or p.maxRain != null -%}
{% if not first %},{% endif %}{% set first = false %}
  {"kind": "Wild patch",
   "label": {{ (generated.items | displayName(p.domain, p.blockCodes[0])) | dump | safe }},
   "url": {{ (('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url ~ 'items/' ~ p.domain ~ '/' ~ (p.blockCodes[0] | slugify) ~ '/') | dump | safe }},
   "minTemp": {{ (p.minTemp if p.minTemp != null else null) | dump | safe }}, "maxTemp": {{ (p.maxTemp if p.maxTemp != null else null) | dump | safe }}, "minRain": {{ (p.minRain if p.minRain != null else null) | dump | safe }}, "maxRain": {{ (p.maxRain if p.maxRain != null else null) | dump | safe }}}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for t in generated.trees -%}
{% if not first %},{% endif %}{% set first = false %}
  {"kind": {{ ("Shrub" if t.isShrub else "Tree") | dump | safe }},
   "label": {{ (generated.items | displayName(t.domain, t.saplingCodes[0]) if (t.saplingCodes and t.saplingCodes.length) else t.generator) | dump | safe }},
   "url": {{ (('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url ~ 'trees/') | dump | safe }},
   "minTemp": {{ (t.minTemp if t.minTemp != null else null) | dump | safe }}, "maxTemp": {{ (t.maxTemp if t.maxTemp != null else null) | dump | safe }}, "minRain": {{ (t.minRain if t.minRain != null else null) | dump | safe }}, "maxRain": {{ (t.maxRain if t.maxRain != null else null) | dump | safe }}}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- for f in generated.fruitTrees -%}
{% if not first %},{% endif %}{% set first = false %}
  {"kind": "Fruit tree",
   "label": {{ (generated.items | displayName(f.domain, f.fruitItemCode) if f.fruitItemCode else f.variety) | dump | safe }},
   "url": {{ (('/' ~ lang ~ '/') | url ~ 'fruit-trees/') | dump | safe }},
   "minTemp": {{ (f.minTemp if f.minTemp != null else null) | dump | safe }}, "maxTemp": {{ (f.maxTemp if f.maxTemp != null else null) | dump | safe }}, "minRain": {{ (f.minRain if f.minRain != null else null) | dump | safe }}, "maxRain": {{ (f.maxRain if f.maxRain != null else null) | dump | safe }}}
{%- endfor -%}
]</script>



